LED: relabel the pin-9 status LED from "red" to "orange" in u-boot.

The board's third status LED is amber/orange (schematic), not red — the upstream
DTS (453) mislabels it. Rename the node + label so the provisioning / recovery env
drives it as `led orange` (matches the kernel DTS relabel and the documented
"orange = attention/waiting" semantics). White/green unchanged.

--- a/arch/arm/dts/openwrt-one.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/openwrt-one.dts
@@ -42,8 +42,8 @@
 		compatible = "gpio-leds";

-		red {
-			label = "red";
+		orange {
+			label = "orange";
 			gpios = <&pio 9 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		};

 		white {
